
## React-Specific

### Architecture
- **Pattern:** {{REACT_PATTERN}} <!-- Functional components / Class components -->
- **State management:** {{STATE_MANAGEMENT}} <!-- Zustand / Redux / Context / None -->
- **Styling:** {{STYLING}} <!-- Tailwind / CSS Modules / styled-components -->
- **Router:** {{ROUTER}} <!-- React Router / Next.js / Expo Router -->

### Key Paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/components/` | Reusable UI components |
| `src/screens/` or `src/pages/` | Route-level components |
| `src/hooks/` | Custom hooks |
| `src/services/` or `src/api/` | API calls and external services |
| `src/stores/` or `src/state/` | State management |
| `src/types/` | TypeScript type definitions |

### Testing
- **Framework:** {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}} <!-- Jest / Vitest / Playwright -->
- **Run all:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
- **Run specific:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}} <path>`
- **Component tests:** Use Testing Library (`@testing-library/react`)

### Style
- **Linter:** ESLint (`npx eslint .`)
- **Formatter:** Prettier (`npx prettier --check .`)
- **Type check:** `npx tsc --noEmit`

### React Conventions
- **Components:** Functional components with hooks (no class components)
- **Props:** Define TypeScript interfaces for all props
- **State:** Colocate state as close to where it's used as possible
- **Effects:** Minimize useEffect — prefer derived state and event handlers
- **Keys:** Never use array index as key for dynamic lists
- **Memoization:** Only `useMemo`/`useCallback` when there's a measured perf issue
